build.reason:
Built under the C10 recipe with the hard no-local-trace rule. The variant gold reads as an ordinary scan over every char and every search char. It keeps no pair, range-end or value-class text, so it has no local trace. Only the existing trigger fails. The pair rule is pinned outside the gold:
- the intact sibling overload StringUtils.containsAny(CharSequence, char[]), called in production by the StringEscapeUtils CSV escaper, with its passing test testContainsAnyCharArrayWithSupplementaryChars;
- StringUtils.contains with testContainsStringWithSupplementaryChars;
- CharSequenceTranslator.translate, which steps through its input by code point.

Files: designs/Lang-31.py, specs/MR-Lang-31.json, instances/MR-Lang-31/{build/*.patch, validation.json} and logs/validate_MR-Lang-31.log.

The recipe applies cleanly. indexOfAny(String, String[]) has no production caller and exactly one test caller, so G5 holds. The original computation splits naturally:
- the facade keeps the guard and places the range [0, length);
- hop 1 decides the empty range;
- hop 2 maps the "none" value to -1;
- hops 3-4 pass the range along;
- the gold owns the per-entry loop.
The null skip is the target's only element-level special-case step. Without it, the gold still reads as an ordinary search with no trace (T1-T4 absent) and is pinned outside the gold:
- the facade javadoc says "A null search array entry will be ignored";
- the sibling lastIndexOfAny skips null entries;
- StringUtils.indexOf and StringUtils.contains treat a null search String as absent;
- passing tests: testLastIndexOfAny_StringStringarray, testIndexOf_String, testContainsString.

toLocale can carry the recipe because the gold is the only method that collects the codes and creates the Locale. No String a hop can hand on lets a gold that keeps the earlier codes return ("us", "EN"): its second code is always the first code followed by the country. The trigger input is valid, so it cannot be pre-filtered, and the Locale is created inside the gold. Every one-line repair above the gold replaces the gold's result, so it is a bypass and is recorded. The country code is checked only by testToLocale_2Part (testToLocale_3Part is empty in this checkout).

External pins:
- the facade javadoc example "en_GB" = new Locale("en", "GB");
- StringUtils.split, which starts each token again after a separator (start = ++i);
- StrTokenizer.tokenize, which clears its work area for every token;
- StringEscapeUtils.unescapeJava, which empties its unicode buffer after each escape (setLength(0)).

Passing ownership tests: testToLocale_1Part, testSplit_StringChar, StrTokenizerTest::testBasic1, testUnescapeJava.
